    "b-sks-rc-evidence-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "EVIDENCE — An "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row is a pinned observation: what was seen, where, at what content state. It is a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " into one of five stores, a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of the captured material, and an optional "
        },
        {
          "insert": "excerpt",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is a content hash of "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", so two claims that lean on the same Discord message cite one row, and the same id resolves to the same material from any subject's page. The pin exists because code and naming drift: the digest fixes what was actually read at citation time. An evidence row claims nothing itself, and citing it does not mean the material states the claim — the connection from observation to claim is the citing fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Facts cite through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact.evidence_ids",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " cites what showed the relation through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link.evidence_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The resolver checks that the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " still resolves and the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "digest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " still matches before a citing row is written, and reconciliation rechecks both later."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-sks-rc-evidence-intro",
      "children": []
    },
